hi,

the config below produces these build failures due to the kmemtrace 
changes:

In file included from include/linux/slub_def.h:14,
                 from include/linux/slab.h:161,
                 from include/linux/percpu.h:6,
                 from 
/home/mingo/tip/arch/x86/include/asm/local.h:5,
                 from include/linux/module.h:21,
                 from include/linux/crypto.h:22,
                 from arch/x86/kernel/asm-offsets_64.c:8,
                 from arch/x86/kernel/asm-offsets.c:5:
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: error: expected ‘)’ before ‘(’ token
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: error: expected ‘)’ before ‘(’ token
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: warning: function declaration isn’t a prototype
include/trace/kmemtrace.h: In function ‘register_trace_kmalloc’:
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: error: ‘probe’ undeclared (first use in this function)
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: error: (Each undeclared identifier is reported only once
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: error: for each function it appears in.)
include/trace/kmemtrace.h: At top level:
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: error: expected ‘)’ before ‘(’ token
include/trace/kmemtrace.h:17: warning: function declaration isn’t a prototype

(Please send a delta patch with the fix as i've already applied your 
patches to tip:tracing/kmemtrace - thanks!)

	Ingo

